I smell fresh bread.
The smell is wonderful.
I find a bakery stall.
A large chalkboard stands next to the stall.
I read the chalkboard.
All the prices are on it.
One Brötchen costs sixty cents.
I step up to the counter.
The trader greets me.
"Good morning, what would you like?" he asks.
"I will take four Brötchen, please," I say.
He packs the Brötchen into a paper bag.
"That makes two euros and forty cents then," the trader says.
I search in my purse.
I have many small coins.
I count the coins.
I pay exactly two euros and forty cents.
"Thank you and have a nice weekend!" the trader says.
"Thank you!" I answer and take the bag.
